    "q-70109": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70109",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Compute the following determinant using a cofactor expansion along the $4$th row:\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Using cofactor expansion along the $4$th row, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =4\\cdot {C}_{41}+0\\cdot {C}_{42}+0\\cdot {C}_{43}+0\\cdot {C}_{44} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{4+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-4|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the $3\\times 3$ determinant by applying a Laplace expansion along the $2$nd row, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =2\\cdot {C}_{21}+0\\cdot {C}_{22}+0\\cdot {C}_{23} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2(9-2) \\\\  & =-14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|=-4\\cdot (-14)=56.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
